.TH GGE\-SAVES 7 "generalGameEngine" "Engine Manual" "Engine Manual"
.SH NAME
gge\-saves \- saving and loading GameState
.SH DESCRIPTION
The save system writes a pointer\-free struct to disk with a header carrying a
version number.
.nf
.ft B
save_write(&e->save, "slot1", g, sizeof *g, SAVE_VERSION);
save_load (&e->save, "slot1", g, sizeof *g, SAVE_VERSION);
save_exists(&e->save, "slot1");
.ft R
.fi
Files live in the per\-user folder derived from
.B EngineConfig.org
and
.B app
(or the working directory when both are NULL).
.SS Rules
GameState must contain no pointers: use fixed arrays and indices. Bump
SAVE_VERSION whenever the struct layout changes; loads of an older version
fail cleanly. Scene statics are not saved, so reset them in
.B on_enter
from the loaded state.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR save_write (3),
.BR save_load (3),
.BR save_exists (3),
.BR gge\-state (7)
